<title>UK: Royal Bank of Scotland sets 150 mln stg FRN.</title>
<headline>Royal Bank of Scotland sets 150 mln stg FRN.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following subordinated perpetual floating-rate issue was announced by lead manager BZW.</p>
<p> BORROWER   ROYAL BANK OF SCOTLAND</p>
<p> AMT    150 MLN STG   SPREAD    *+50 BP    MATURITY  * PERPETUAL</p>
<p> TYPE	 FRN	 BASE	 3M LIBOR  PAY DATE    26.MAR.97</p>
<p> LAST MOODY A1	  ISS PRICE  99.39     FULL FEES   50 BP</p>
<p> LAST S&amp;P   A	   REOFFER    99.39</p>
<p> NOTES	*CALL FROM 25.MAR.07 AFTER WHICH SPREAD STEPS UP TO</p>
<p>		 +150 BP</p>
<p> LISTING    LONDON    DENOMS (K) 100	 SALE LIMITS US/UK</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   IPMA (2)</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY  =	   TAX PROVS   STD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.25	SELL CONC  0.25	PRAECIP     =</p>
<p> NOTES	ISSUED OFF THE MTN PROGRAMME</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8863</p>
</text>
